# Documentation


- **Get started**
- [Overview](/docs/): Welcome to Urlbox, an API for converting URLs and HTML into screenshots, PDFs, videos, and extracting text, html and metadata with ease.
- [Quick Start](/docs/quickstart): Quickly learn how to use Urlbox's website screenshot API
- [Projects](/docs/projects): Learn about Projects and how to use them.

- **Capture**
- [Screenshots](/docs/screenshots): Capture full-page screenshots and target specific elements on a page.
- Videos
  - [Recording videos](/docs/videos/recording-videos): How to record MP4 and WebM videos of any website with Urlbox, including scrolling videos and section-controlled scrolling
- [PDFs](/docs/pdfs): Render web pages and HTML to PDF.
- [Render Links](/docs/render-links): Create screenshots, PDFs and other renders by embedding a single link in your HTML or emails.
- Saving to S3
  - [Saving to S3](/docs/storage): Persist renders directly into your own cloud storage bucket.
  - [Configuring S3](/docs/storage/configure-s3): Save your screenshots, PDFs and other renders to an S3 bucket from Urlbox
  - [Configuring a private S3 bucket](/docs/storage/configure-s3-private): Save your screenshots, PDFs and other renders to a private S3 bucket from Urlbox
  - [Configuring Cloudflare R2](/docs/storage/configure-cloudflare-r2): Save your screenshots, PDFs and other renders to a Cloudflare R2 bucket from Urlbox
  - [Configuring Google Cloud Storage](/docs/storage/configure-google-cloud-storage): Save your screenshots, PDFs and other renders to Google Cloud Storage from Urlbox
  - [Configuring Digital Ocean Spaces](/docs/storage/configure-digitalocean-spaces): Save your screenshots, PDFs and other renders to a Digital Ocean Spaces bucket from Urlbox
  - [Configuring Backblaze B2](/docs/storage/configure-backblaze-b2): Save your screenshots, PDFs and other renders to a Backblaze B2 bucket from Urlbox
  - [Configuring Azure Blob Storage](/docs/storage/configure-azure-blob-storage): Save your screenshots, PDFs and other renders to an Azure Blob Storage container from Urlbox

