- **Agents & CLI**
- AI agents (MCP)
  - [Overview](/docs/agents): Connect Claude, ChatGPT, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, VS Code or any other MCP client to Urlbox by adding one URL and signing in with your Urlbox account.
  - [Connect your agent](/docs/agents/mcp): Add the Urlbox MCP server to Claude, ChatGPT, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, VS Code or any other MCP client, and sign in with your Urlbox account.
  - [Signing in](/docs/agents/authentication): Sign in to the Urlbox MCP server with your Urlbox account, manage connections, and choose which project renders use. API keys are a fallback for headless use.
  - [Tools and prompts](/docs/agents/tools): Every tool and prompt the Urlbox MCP server offers, what each needs, and how long renders work.
  - [Using the CLI from an AI agent](/docs/cli/ai-agents)
- Urlbox CLI
  - [Overview](/docs/cli): Render screenshots, PDFs and videos from your terminal with the Urlbox CLI, or hand it to an AI agent and have a screenshot saved in under a minute.
  - [Quickstart](/docs/cli/quickstart): Install the Urlbox CLI and render screenshots, PDFs and more from your terminal.
  - [Install & update](/docs/cli/install): Install the Urlbox CLI with npm, Homebrew, Scoop or the install script, verify it with urlbox doctor, and keep it current with urlbox upgrade.
  - [Authentication](/docs/cli/authentication): Sign in to the Urlbox CLI with urlbox login, switch orgs and projects, and authenticate CI and headless environments with an env var.
  - [Rendering](/docs/cli/rendering): Capture screenshots, PDFs and videos from the terminal with the Urlbox CLI, covering formats, presets, viewport, full-page, and the common render flags.
  - [Saving files & output](/docs/cli/output-and-scripting): Control where the Urlbox CLI saves renders with the --output sandbox, and choose how each command's result is printed.
  - [Any option with --json](/docs/cli/json-and-schema): Use --json to pass any Urlbox API option through the CLI, even ones without a dedicated flag.
  - [Signed render links](/docs/cli/signed-links): Generate signed Urlbox render URLs locally with urlbox link, with no API call and no credit spent, to embed in templates, emails and websites.
  - [Async renders & webhooks](/docs/cli/async-and-webhooks): Queue heavy Urlbox renders with --async and receive the result by webhook, or check on a render with urlbox status.
  - [Screenshots from a CSV](/docs/cli/batch-csv): Render a whole list of URLs from a CSV into a folder with the Urlbox CLI, by asking an AI agent or with a short shell loop.
  - [Using the CLI from an AI agent](/docs/cli/ai-agents): Install the Urlbox agent skill so Claude Code, Cursor, Codex or opencode can drive the CLI for you and render in plain English.
  - [Storage, proxies & LLMs](/docs/cli/org-resources): Manage your organisation's storage credentials, proxies and LLM credentials from the Urlbox CLI, and assign them to projects.
  - [Configuration](/docs/cli/configuration): Where the Urlbox CLI stores its configuration, how to read and change it, and how env vars fit in.
  - [Troubleshooting](/docs/cli/troubleshooting): Diagnose Urlbox CLI problems with urlbox doctor and understand the error codes it reports.
  - [Command reference](/docs/cli/command-reference): Every Urlbox CLI command and global flag in one place, from render, screenshot and link to login, projects, storage and doctor.

- **Help**
- Guides
  - [Guides](/docs/guides): Step-by-step Urlbox guides for bulk screenshots, proxies, avoiding blocks, logged-in pages, local URLs, saving to S3, thumbnails and side renders.
  - [Taking screenshots of all pages on a website](/docs/guides/bulk-website-screenshots)
  - [Proxies](/docs/guides/proxies): Learn how to configure a proxy with Urlbox
  - [Static IP for whitelisting](/docs/guides/static-ip): Render from a fixed Urlbox IP address that you can allowlist on your firewall, WAF or staging site
  - [Avoiding Being Blocked](/docs/guides/avoiding-being-blocked): Detect block pages and CAPTCHAs, retry blocked renders automatically, and use stealth and proxies to capture the real content
  - [Setting the User Agent](/docs/guides/setting-the-user-agent): How to override the default user agent
  - [Saving to S3](/docs/guides/s3)
  - [Sandbox](/docs/guides/sandbox): The Urlbox sandbox is a place for you to play around with the various options available in the API before coding your integration.
  - [Side Renders](/docs/guides/side-renders): Generate extra artifacts - HTML, MHTML, markdown, metadata, extracted content and thumbnails - from the same page load as your main render
  - [Rendering thumbnails](/docs/guides/thumbnails): Generate multiple thumbnail images from a single render using the thumbnails option
  - [Rendering Behind a Login](/docs/guides/rendering-behind-login): How to screenshot pages that require you to be logged in, using session cookies or auth headers
  - [Rendering Local URLs](/docs/guides/rendering-local-urls): How to render sites running on localhost or a private network by exposing them through a tunnel
- Example Code
  - [Example Code](/docs/examplecode): Code samples for taking website screenshots with Urlbox in Node.js, Ruby, Python, PHP, Java and C#, using the official SDKs or plain HTTP.
  - [Node.js website screenshots](/docs/examplecode/node): Take website screenshots in Node.js with Urlbox — signed render links for img tags, sync renders for scripts, and async renders with webhooks.
  - [Ruby website screenshots](/docs/examplecode/ruby): Generate website screenshots with Ruby and Rails
  - [Python website screenshots](/docs/examplecode/python): Take website screenshots in Python and Django with the Urlbox SDK — signed render links for templates, direct downloads, and async renders with webhooks.
  - [PHP website screenshots](/docs/examplecode/php): Take website screenshots in PHP and Laravel with the Urlbox SDK — signed render links, sync renders saved to disk, and async renders with verified webhooks.
  - [Java website screenshots](/docs/examplecode/java): URL to image with Java
  - [C# website screenshots](/docs/examplecode/csharp): Generate website screenshots with C#
- Common Problems
  - [Common Problems](/docs/common-problems): Fixes for the most common Urlbox rendering problems — blocked or blank screenshots, missing content, broken full-page captures — and the options most people set.
  - [Most-used options](/docs/common-problems/most-used-options): The options most people set on almost every render.
  - [Avoiding blocks](/docs/common-problems/avoiding-blocks): Fix blank or blocked screenshots caused by bot detection, Cloudflare, or 403s.
  - [Getting complete renders](/docs/common-problems/getting-complete-renders): Fix screenshots captured too early that miss late-loading content.
  - [Full-page gotchas](/docs/common-problems/full-page-gotchas): Fix full-page screenshots that are cut off, stretched, or have duplicated headers.
  - [Saving to your storage](/docs/common-problems/saving-to-storage): Send renders to your own bucket, or get notified with a webhook.
- [LLMs.txt](/docs/llms.txt)